        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Decanuclear Dy6Zn4 cluster is an SMM under zero dc field. χMT is slightly below the six-DyIII free-ion value at 300 K and decreases on cooling, consistent with weak antiferromagnetic coupling (θ = −2.9 K) and/or Stark depopulation. Magnetization at 5 T is well below the hexanuclear Dy theoretical limit. Fully formed in-phase and out-of-phase AC signals (ca. 3–15 K) give Ueff = 43 K and τ0 = 1 × 10−5 s, with a secondary lower-temperature relaxation pathway.",
